@startuml
' Shared notation key for the SAD (Figure 2). Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
' It is a small, illustrative fragment that shows every notation the views use:
' the four element fills, the queue and store shapes, the provided-interface lollipop
' (a port), and each connector type including the one-way event stream.
!include style.puml
title Diagram key: notation legend (illustrative C&C fragment)

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 30

actor "Manager" as MGR
node "POS system" as POS #6FA8DC
component "POS Adapter" as PA #6FA8DC
component "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
queue "Outbox" as OB #8E7CC3
component "Communications\nFront-End\n(pub-sub event bus)" as CFE #F1C232
interface "IEP" as IEPIF
component "Subscriber" as SUB #F1C232

MGR --> SA : <<request/reply>>\ninventory query
POS --> PA : <<event stream>>\nsales records (one way)
PA --> SA : <<local call>>\nInventory Events
SA --> SLI : <<data access>>\napply, read
SA --> OB : <<data access>>\nappend (ordered)
CFE -- IEPIF
OB --> IEPIF : <<pub-sub>> publish\nIEP / TLS 1.3 [secure]
IEPIF --> OB : <<pub-sub>> acknowledge
CFE --> SUB : <<pub-sub>> notify
SUB --> CFE : <<pub-sub>> ack (cursor)

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| green fill | store-side runtime component |
| gold fill | distribution-center runtime component |
| blue fill | external system or boundary element |
| purple queue / database | durable, ordered persistent store |
| stick figure | human role (manager), not a component |
| circle on a stalk (lollipop) | a provided interface or port a connector attaches to |
| solid arrow | connector; the label names the type and protocol |
| <<pub-sub>> | the n-ary publish-subscribe connector (the IEP) |
| <<event stream>> | a one-way stream of events (no reply) |
| <<request/reply>> | a synchronous request and reply |
| <<data access>> | a component reading or writing its own store |
| <<local call>> | an in-process hand-off between a component and its boundary element |
| [secure] | a store-to-DC network leg carried over TLS 1.3 with mutual certificates |
endlegend
@enduml
